To find the frequency of letters in a given string, you can use the following Java code:

```java
public static void frequency(String str) {
    // Get the length of the string
    int n = str.length();

    // Initialize the frequency array with zeros
    int[] freq = new int[26];

    // Calculate the frequency of each character in the string
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        freq[str.charAt(i) - 'a']++;
    }

    // Print the characters with their frequencies
    for (int i = 0; i < 26; i++) {
        // Print only those characters whose frequency is not 0
        if (freq[i] != 0) {
            System.out.print((char)(i + 'a'));
            System.out.print(freq[i] + " ");
        }
    }
}
```

In this code, we start by initializing an integer array, `freq`, of size 26. This array will be used to store the frequency of each character in the given string. We then iterate over each character in the string and increment the corresponding frequency in the `freq` array.

Finally, we iterate over the `freq` array and print the characters (converted from ASCII to characters using `(char)(i + 'a')`) along with their respective frequencies, only if the frequency is not 0.

This code will output the frequency of each letter in the given string.

