Here is the Java program that compares two strings lexicographically and returns the index of the first different character:

```java
public class CompareStrings {
    public static int compareStrings(String string1, String string2) {
        // Check if either string is null
        if (string1 == null || string2 == null) {
            return -2;
        }

        // Get the length of the shorter string
        int minLength = Math.min(string1.length(), string2.length());

        // Compare each character of the strings
        for (int i = 0; i < minLength; i++) {
            if (string1.charAt(i) != string2.charAt(i)) {
                return i;
            }
        }

        // If the strings have different lengths, return the length of the shorter string
        if (string1.length() != string2.length()) {
            return minLength;
        }

        // If the strings are equal, return -1
        return -1;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String string1 = "GeeksforGeeks";
        String string2 = "GeeksGforGeks";
        int index = compareStrings(string1, string2);
